 {qtype:"Matching Features", instr:"Look at the following statements and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D.", optKey:"letter",
  options:["A  Helena Marsh","B  Rafael Ostrowski","C  Nadia Farouk","D  Gareth Lowe"],
  items:[
  {q:"The participants in the trial may not be representative of employers in general.", a:"B", ev:"cannot be considered typical of businesses as a whole", ex:"Ostrowski argues that confident volunteers are not typical. 'Representative' paraphrases 'typical'."},
  {q:"Reducing working days could lead to greater pressure on employees.", a:"C", ev:"A shorter week, she warns, can easily become a more intense one", ex:"Farouk warns of work intensification. Although she supports shorter hours in principle, this statement matches her warning."},
  {q:"The evidence supports a far broader adoption of the four-day week.", a:"A", ev:"the findings are strong enough to justify introducing the four-day week much more widely", ex:"Marsh, who led the research, believes the results justify wider introduction."},
  {q:"Very small businesses might struggle with the cost of the arrangement.", a:"D", ev:"without hiring people they cannot afford", ex:"Lowe doubts that firms with a handful of staff can afford to cover the extra day off."}
 ]}
